# Build context is ./backend (see src/SmartReptile.Api/Dockerfile). This file is REQUIRED for correctness,
# not just speed: without it `COPY src/ src/` overwrites the Linux restore output produced inside the image
# with whatever the developer's machine left in obj/. On Windows that assets file hard-codes
# C:\Users\<user>\.nuget\packages\ paths, so `dotnet publish --no-restore` fails in the container with
# NETSDK1064 ("package was not found ... might have been deleted since NuGet restore") even though every
# package is present. Verified by reproducing that exact failure, then fixing it with this file.

**/bin/
**/obj/
**/TestResults/
**/publish/

# Tooling / editor noise that must never reach the image.
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user
*.suo
*.DotSettings.user

# Local secrets and environment overrides.
.env
*.env
!*.env.example
appsettings.Local.json
*.pfx
*.p12
*.snk
